scription":"Besides, we also tested the logP values of oxaliplatin, complexes 12 and complex 14 via shaking method and determined with HPLC instrument, using the same chromatographic conditions mentioned above. Firstly, the standard curves of oxaliplatin, compound 12 and complex 14 were obtained from HPLC and graphed with GraphPad 8.0. As for the assays of partition coefficient, oxaliplatin (50 mg) or complexes 12/14 (50 mg) was added into equilibrium glass bottles which containing a fixed mass ratio of deionized water (5 mL) and n-octanol (5 mL) then the solution was agitated for 12 h, 24 h or 36 h at 25 °C in dark. After that, the solutions centrifuged at 5000 r/min for 10 min, collected the upper or lower portion and diluted to desired concentration. The contents each portion were determined via HPLC instrument with the same chromatographic conditions mentioned above in section 4.9. Partition coefficient values were obtained via the formula: P=Co/Cw. Co represented concentrations 14 in n-octanol, while Cw represented concentrations in water."}]}